<urn:atm:triage:finding/AN6-TESTQUALITY-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AN6-TESTQUALITY-001" ;
  triage:title "parameterized_query_returns_column_labelled_rows lost equality-selectivity coverage" ;
  triage:description "AN6-RULE008-003-FIX-2 (3c62c2bb389061ee820c99aa5971300dd05f7cb2) fixed a RULE-008/009 identity-literal violation by rewriting the test predicate from team-equals-question-mark to team-not-equals-question-mark and binding a synthetic non-matching value (TEST_NONEXISTENT_TEAM equals test-team). Confirmed by quality-mgr (AN6-QA-6): since all 4 fixture rows share team equals atm-dev and no fixture row matches test-team, the not-equals predicate returns all 4 rows for any bound string value, so the test no longer distinguishes correct equality-parameter-binding from broken or ignored binding (a null binding would still be caught). This is a real coverage loss on the equality-selectivity path, not a fabricated pass; identities/lint/clippy/tests are all genuinely green. Recommended remediation (either): add a second distinct team value to the atm-storage-rusqlite analyst-query fixture and restore equals semantics, or reference an already-allowlisted production-canonical literal as the equality target instead of inverting to not-equals." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-an" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "test-quality" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
